What each switch does (Common::PeSwitch, exactly "1"; read once):
EDEN_UP_L949_ACQUIRE=1: a greater-or-equal Switch 2 acquire (ProcessSemaphoreTriggerMethod) and
  the polls of a suspended one (CanResumeAcquire) are decided without draining the back
  (CheckWithoutDrain): met by the word in memory, or by the last release the front queued to that
  word while the back has not run it (GpuSplit::QueuedSemaphoreWriteAt; it then NoteSyncs). The
  front records each semaphore write as it sends it (GpuSplit::NoteSemaphoreWrite, by device
  address, payload or "unknown"): puller releases (WriteLong and its Switch 2 mirror, legacy
  release, SEM_EXECUTE release), 3D report_semaphore releases/report-only (FrontWrite,
  FrontCallMultiMethod; counters and reductions are "unknown"), compute SET_REPORT_SEMAPHORE_D
  (FrontCallMethod, FrontCallMultiMethod, FrontRunMacro), copy engine LAUNCH_DMA releases
  (DmaPusher::NoteDmaSemaphore). Left to the T83 path (drain, or SEM_FAST's read if set): equal and
  mask acquires, an unmapped word or one on a GPU-written page, an unknown or unmatched queued
  write, macros on the back, delayed fences or High GPU accuracy. With fence-flagged releases held
  until their host fence (EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1, or EDEN_NX2_READBACK_WAIT=2/3; the play
  env sets KEEP_PENDING=0 and has no READBACK_WAIT) a queued release never passes an acquire: it
  counts as not met until it lands (review fix, see Review below). An unmet first check drains as
  before (as upstream); an unmet poll keeps waiting without a drain, resumes on a latch, and drains
  once per 1 ms (the valve; it also logs waits over 2 s as before). Basis: Switch 2 sync words only
  advance, so a value met now stays met once the back ran the queued work.
EDEN_UP_L949_DRAIN_VALVE=1: the same 1 ms valve for EDEN_NX2_SEM_FAST's drain-free polls (SEM_FAST
  drains once after 2 s, then never: the shape that hung Mario Kart World upstream). Nothing
  without SEM_FAST; L949_ACQUIRE has the valve built in.
EDEN_UP_SHIP2_FEED=1: the back stores where it ran dry (back_idle_at); Commit publishes once the
  front holds 8 unpublished words while the back waits there, instead of at publish_every (up to
  256 between drains). The GPU thread's pending-channel loop asks a back that ran everything and
  has not run its idle hook for it (SettleIdleBack), as a poll's drain did, without waiting.
  Changed from ship2-feed.diff: "=2" (feed without settle) dropped, its counter line moved to
  EDEN_UP_L949_STATS, switch read with PeSwitch.
EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP=1 (needs EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1, else inert): a delta draw binds a small
  streamed uniform buffer (BindSmallUniformReusing path, <= 4 KiB) from the stream allocation the
  previous draw made for the same stage, slot, address and size in the same command buffer,
  without reading guest memory, when nothing between the two draws wrote its range: no rebind of
  the slot or inline constant data over it (the delta's binds and device ranges), no CPU write the
  cache was told about (WriteMemory, CachedWriteMemory), no GPU-modified mark (MarkWrittenBuffer,
  DMACopy), no buffer deleted, at most 8 such writes. Only delta draws keep, so it acts on ~11-13%
  of Ocarina's draws with FAST_DRAW_OOT_EXEMPT (t78-x: 2,250-2,643 of ~20,500 draws/s).
EDEN_UP_L949_DESC_REPLAY=1 (needs EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1, else inert): the resolve that captures
  delta_views keeps the image descriptor entries it pushed per stage and its rescaling words;
  delta draws copy them into the descriptor queue (UpdateDescriptorQueue::AddEntries) instead of
  looking up every view, sampler, handle and rescale bit again. Dropped on a new capture or when
  any image changed scale (TextureCache::ScaleEpoch, counted in InvalidateScale). Same delta-draw
  share as above. Both fast draw pieces do nothing under EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_VERIFY (no draw takes
  the delta path there).
Diagnostics: EDEN_UP_L949_STATS=1 logs every 10 s "Lichii #949 in 10 s (...): acquires P passed
  without a drain (Q by a queued release), K met by a queued release held until its fence (not
  passed), L resumed by a latch, O left to the old path (reasons),
  V valve drains, W polls waited without a drain, S SEM_FAST valve drains; polls: ...; back: B
  waits for work, X ms spinning, H idle hooks (ms), Z sleeps (ms); E early publishes, T idle hooks
  asked by polls", plus "uniform keeps in 600 frames" and "delta descriptors in 10 s" when those
  are on. No behaviour change, so give it to the control too. EDEN_UP_L949_ACQUIRE_VERIFY=1,
  EDEN_UP_L949_UBO_KEEP_VERIFY=1, EDEN_UP_L949_DESC_REPLAY_VERIFY=1: drain/bind/resolve the old
  way as well and count differences (verify runs only, slow).

Deviations from upstream: everything is behind the switches above (upstream is always on); its
counters ran with EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE, here only with EDEN_UP_L949_STATS (a GPU_PROFILE run with
the switches unset stays as T83); counter "drained" is "left to the old path" (SEM_FAST may
answer those without a drain); the Switch 2 mirror release is noted too; our TakeReusableDraw reads
the delta in place, so only its binds and device ranges are copied (taken_delta), and only with
UBO_KEEP; the keep check comes after the EDEN_UP_UBO_SNAPSHOT path (which keeps precedence) and
there are no keeps with EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_BANKFLAG=1 (that switch exists for guest CPU writes the
caches don't know yet); with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW an acquire passed without a drain sends an empty
deferred call, which ends delta reuse at the acquire in stream order as the drained path's flush
did (not upstream: the CPU may have rewritten what the next draws read before its release);
UpdateDescriptorQueue::UpdateCount added (upstream had it); a queued release does not pass an
acquire while releases are held until their fence (ReleasesHeldUntilFence, our tree's
QUERY_KEEP_PENDING and READBACK_WAIT; upstream's ReleasesLandAtOnce only knows the fence
settings). Not ported: the 64-slot lock-free
waiter table (8056420f5b): upstream's reason was MKW's ~85k polls/s; Latched's mutex is held for
a few ns and the back's OnWrite takes it only while a channel waits, so no measurable cost here.

Unset (all switches): T83 behaviour. What still runs: one false test in Commit, SettleIdleBack's
early return, BackLoop's two false tests per wait, the note helpers' switch checks, the slot's
device_addr store in BindSmallUniformReusing and BindSmallUniformFromSource (read only by the
keep), ++scale_epoch in InvalidateScale, a buffer deletion
counter, and new struct members (PendingAcquire::last_drain, Slot::device_addr, ...).

Risks: L949_ACQUIRE passes an acquire early if a queued write the front does not record lowers a
word (inline uploads, 2D/inline-to-memory, a compute engine run on the back, guest-memory QMD
releases), i.e. if the "sync words only advance" basis fails; the front's record only knows the
payload word and the zero high word of a timed release, not its timestamp words (+8, +12). Without
held releases a fence-flagged queued release meets an acquire before its value lands (upstream's
verify counts ~820 per 10 s at the Bananza gate as "met by a queued release not in memory after
it", by design; the play env's case); with them (KEEP_PENDING=1, READBACK_WAIT=2/3) it does not.
The valve adds up to 1,000 drains/s
per waiting channel. SHIP2_FEED publishes more often (a seq_cst store each) while the back keeps
pace, and the settle runs the deferred submit earlier. L949_ACQUIRE without SHIP2_FEED: polls stop
draining, so a back that ran dry spins its 8192 PAUSEs (~0.2-0.3 ms) before its deferred submit:
test them together (upstream ships them together). UBO_KEEP misses a guest CPU write the caches
were not told about between two draws of one delta chain (upstream's stated assumption; with the
full frame wait the game is blocked while those draws run). DESC_REPLAY reuses VkImageView and
VkSampler handles within a delta chain; deletions, texture cache writes and unmaps end the chain,
and ScaleEpoch catches rescales. Not stacked-checked with lichii-956.diff (EDEN_UP_ACQUIRE_NO_DRAIN,
parked, not in T83): both replace SEM_FAST's read at the same sites; don't enable both.

Expected (Ocarina, docked full res, full frame wait): +0 to +0.3 fps (0 to +2%) for the whole set,
best guess ~+0.1 fps, below the ~0.5 fps run noise. Upstream measured +1.2-1.4 fps (+8-9%) at the
Bananza gate (5900X, back thread 56.0 -> 52.2 ms per frame): acquire+feed alone +0.7 (+5%), uniform
keeps +0.4 (+3%), descriptor replay +0.2 (noise), with ~85-109k delta draws/s. Here: t74-d cut
front drains 17.1k -> 3.5k/s (SEM_FAST + DMA_SNAPSHOT + DRAIN_SKIP_SAME) with drain time ~unchanged
(497 -> 464 ms/s), back idle 262-349 vs 262-401 ms/s and fps the same: the back is the limit while
the frame wait holds the game 46 of 73 ms per frame, so drains saved move to other waits. The
acquire part removes ~1-2.4k acquire drains/s (~92-128 ms/s of front waiting in profiled T75 walks) on
top of DMA_SNAPSHOT: 0 to +1%. Feed and settle can only take the publish and idle-hook latency off
the back's path (<= ~0.1-0.3 ms per frame): 0 to +0.5%. Uniform keeps and descriptor replay act on
~2.5k delta draws/s, ~40x fewer than at the Bananza gate: < +0.3%, and fast draw itself measured
11.6-11.8 vs 12.0-12.2 fps (t78-x).

