Readouts: walk fps mean and 1% low, flashes/min, pond load OK; "Lichii #949 in 10 s": passed vs
left to the old path (a, w: most greater-or-equal acquires pass; "held until its fence" stays 0 in
the play env, KEEP_PENDING=0; c counts no acquire decisions at
all, only its polls and back lines, the baseline for back waits / spinning / idle hooks / sleeps),
valve drains, early publishes, idle hooks asked by polls. A met poll is decided twice (the
scheduler's look, then ResumeAcquire), so passed/latched/acquire polls count resumed polls twice;
compare arms, not absolute numbers. "GPU split per second" (SPLIT_WAITS): front waited and the
acquire / acquire poll / acquire recheck sites, back idle; w: "uniform keeps in 600 frames" kept
vs streamed, "delta descriptors in 10 s" replayed vs pushed; v: "acquire verify" passed-but-not-met
= 0 (met by a queued release not in memory may be > 0, by design; 0 with QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1),
uniform keep verify mismatches = 0, delta descriptors verify mismatches = 0.
Optional, only with a SEM_FAST retest: EDEN_NX2_SEM_FAST=1 vs EDEN_NX2_SEM_FAST=1
EDEN_UP_L949_DRAIN_VALVE=1 ("SEM_FAST valve drains" > 0, no hang).

Review (9 Nov, adversarial pass; original kept as lichii-949.diff.pre-review): fixed one defect,
latent in the current play env (it sets QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=0), live in any arm that sets it to 1.
EDEN_NX2_QUERY_KEEP_PENDING=1 and EDEN_NX2_READBACK_WAIT=2/3 make fence-flagged
releases land only when their host fence pops (FenceManager::SignalFenceImpl delays them through
g_signaling_query_report_fence), which ReleasesLandAtOnce (fence settings only) did not know: a
queued release passed the acquire (MetByQueued) where T83 waits until it landed, so timed releases
(written at once) after the acquire could reach the CPU before the held one, the order
KEEP_PENDING exists to keep. Now such an acquire is met by memory if memory already meets it, else
not met ("held" count): the first check drains as T83, polls wait for the query cache's latch or the
1 ms valve. Hardening: BindSmallUniformFromSource (EDEN_UP_UBO_SNAPSHOT) marks its slot as from no
address, so a keep never rebinds a snapshot copy as a guest-memory read (it shares the slots and
left device_addr stale). Header: control arm readouts and the double-counted polls corrected.
Checked, no change
needed: unset = T83 (all new code behind false switch tests), PendingAcquire/Slot member order,
static_vector bounds (8 + 64 <= 72), descriptor replay counts equal the pipeline's pushes, no new
lock order, CB data reaches memory_writes through InnerInvalidation (more than 8 ranges between two
draws turn keeps off for that draw: an effect limit, not a defect).

